# Copy snippets into each service’s `.env` as needed.
# Default ports when running `npm run dev` from repo root (all services at once):

# Run all backends: from repo root →  npm run dev
#
# payments    → http://localhost:4100  (v1 docs: /v1/api-docs, v2: /v2/api-docs, Socket.IO)
# preferences → http://localhost:3001 (/api-docs)
# providers   → http://localhost:4000 (/api-docs)
# coupons     → http://localhost:3002 (/api-docs, /metrics)
# utils       → http://localhost:3030 (main API + WebSocket), http://localhost:4030 (email routes)
# reviews     → http://localhost:5005
#
# Web UI: second terminal:
#   cp apps/servase-ui/.env.local.example apps/servase-ui/.env.local
#   Set REACT_APP_PAYMENTS_URL=http://localhost:4100 so the UI calls local payments, not
#   a deployed host (e.g. Render). Restart the dev server after editing .env.local.
#   then:  npm run dev:ui
#
# Admin dashboard (Settings, Payments, pricing) — same value as utils ADMIN_PUSH_SECRET:
#   REACT_APP_ADMIN_PUSH_SECRET=your-local-dev-secret
#   (local dev: serveaso-test-push-secret matches backend default)
#
# preferences (services/preferences/.env) — MONGO_URI required. Match payments/utils, or
#   local: MONGO_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017
#   See services/preferences/.env.example
#
# DATABASE_URL (Postgres) / Razorpay / Twilio: see each service’s own config or .env.example.
#
# Postgres database name (all services): copy to repo-root `.env.local` — see `.env.local.example`
#   POSTGRES_DB=serveaso1
#   docker compose up -d && npm run dev:setup
